WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.900
1943.

2
00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:05.220
A teenage soldier watches
his home city, Hamburg,

3
00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.320
destroyed by bombing.

4
00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:12.460
Later, as a prisoner of war, he comes
to faith reading the Bible in the camp.

5
00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:15.490
He became the theologian Jürgen Moltmann.

6
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:20.080
Yet for centuries, most Christian
theologians taught that God cannot be changed

7
00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.520
by anything outside God.

8
00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:26.430
When Jesus died on the
cross, did God suffer too?

9
00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:31.690
In this mission, you'll set Bible texts
about an unchanging God beside texts where

10
00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.190
God grieves.

11
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:37.590
Then you'll weigh up what a suffering
God would mean for people in pain.

12
00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:42.680
Your mission: find out whether, and
how, Christians think God can suffer.
